  "content": {
    "id": "p50-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Show that $x^2-(2q+1)x+q(q+1)=0$ always yields consecutive integer solutions for all integer $q$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\Delta=1$, so $x=q$ or $x=q+1$. These are consecutive integers for every integer $q$.",
      "worked": "$a=1$, $b=-(2q+1)$, $c=q(q+1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-(2q+1))^2-4(1)q(q+1)\\\\\\Delta&=4q^2+4q+1-4q^2-4q\\\\\\Delta&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThe solutions are\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{2q+1\\pm\\sqrt{1}}{2}\\\\x&=\\frac{2q+1\\pm1}{2}\\\\x&=q+1\\text{ or }q\\end{align*}$$\nFor integer $q$, both roots are integers and differ by $1$, so they are consecutive integers.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
